-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock: Soul Shard generation talents
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- Three talents that grant a Soul Shard on a proc.  All three share one
-- AuraScript (spell_warl_shard_on_proc, src/WarlockShardGain.cpp); the
-- conditions live entirely in spell_proc.
--
--   Intensity     -> Burning Soul  (18135/18136)
--       "Critical hits from your fire spells have an X% chance to generate a
--        Soul Shard."  Gated purely by spell_proc: HitMask = 2 (critical),
--        SchoolMask = 4 (fire), Chance = 15/30.
--       NOTE: talent 829 "Intensity" (TabID 282) is a DIFFERENT talent that
--       shares the name -- it is deliberately not touched.
--
--   Aftermath     (18119/18120)
--       "Increases the periodic damage on your Immolate by X%, and Immolate
--        periodic damage has a chance equal to your critical strike chance to
--        generate a Soul Shard."
--       Effect2 (ADD_PCT_MODIFIER / MiscValue 22 = SPELLMOD_DOT, mask B1 = 4
--       = Immolate) is KEPT and buffed from 3%/7% to 10%/20%.  Effect1 becomes
--       a DUMMY proc carrier.  spell_proc Chance = 100; the real gate is the
--       crit-chance roll in C++, which spell_proc cannot express.
--       The old Conflagrate daze half (trigger 18118) is dropped.
--
--   Demonic Power -> Molten Rain  (18126/18127)
--       "Rain of Fire has an X% chance to generate a Soul Shard from each
--        enemy hit."  Cooldown = 0 so it can fire per target per tick --
--        that is what makes "from each enemy hit" fall out for free.
--
-- ProcFlags = 0 / ProcChance = 101 on every talent rank so that spell_proc is
-- the sole gate.  SpellPhaseMask = 2 everywhere: a spell_proc row with
-- SpellPhaseMask = 0 silently never triggers.
-- ===========================================================================


